  "body": "## Reproduction\n\nCreate a millimetre DXF with a closed sketch in ENTITIES. Add empty model-space and paper-space definitions to BLOCKS. The file can also contain a root DICTIONARY and empty child dictionaries in OBJECTS. These records do not add sketch geometry.\n\nImport the file on a setup with stock. The importer stops at the first BLOCK. A file with the same ENTITIES and an empty BLOCKS section can also fail on OBJECTS.\n\n## Expected result\n\nAccept a bounded, validated subset of empty reserved layout definitions and empty dictionary trees. Import the same geometry, units and placement as the file without these records. Keep the diagnostic for unsupported geometry, block instances, semantic objects and invalid record structures. Use original synthetic fixtures.\n\nThis is separate from expansion of authored BLOCK and INSERT geometry in #1865. It affects the stock-face sketch workflow in #1452 and #2022.\n\nSuggested labels: bug, P3, effort:high, area:2d, source:agent.\n",
